"""Create captions and a hash manifest from the completed W-C figure numbers."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
import pandas as pd
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];O=ROOT/'paper/figs/r2c'
f=json.loads((O/'fig_numbers.json').read_text());p=json.loads((ROOT/'analysis/r2c/primary.json').read_text())['primaries']
_src=pd.read_parquet(ROOT/'runs/r2c1/scored.parquet',columns=['critical_source']).critical_source.value_counts()
ARB=int(_src.get('arbiter',0));FB=int(_src.get('J1',0)+_src.get('J2',0))
FBTXT=(f'Critical J1/J2 disagreements were resolved by the post-hoc cross-family arbiter ({ARB} scored rows; analysis/r2c/arbitration.md); {FB} fallback rows remain.' if ARB else 'Fallback critical J1/J2 labels are unresolved, not definitive labels.')
ARBTXT=(' The production scoring fallback was replaced by post-hoc arbitration (unknown-masked snapshot: analysis/r2c/snapshot_unknown_masked/).' if ARB else ' The production scoring fallback has no completed arbiter file.')
def pct(x):return f'{100*x:.2f}%'
text=['# W-C publication figures\n',
'All six figures are available as vector PDF and 600-dpi PNG. Inputs: runs/r2c1/scored.parquet and data/items/r2_c1.jsonl / r2_c2.jsonl. P0 primary outcomes; 238 families after D-018 exclusions. Bars/lines pool the four fixed models; open markers show individual models where indicated. All intervals are pointwise 95% percentile CIs from 10,000 recorded seed/construction-cluster resamples, seed 20261031. '+FBTXT+'\n',
'Provenance qualification: 48 generation requests reuse caches older than the final item freeze, including 12 primary requests. All primary generation timestamps postdate the PREREG mtime; the final item freeze did not precede every cached generation. No claim of an unqualified wholly fresh confirmation.'+ARBTXT+' Registered contrasts, missingness, Holm inference and sensitivity analyses are in analysis/r2c/report.md and primary.json.\n',
'## fig_defaults\n\nBare P0 semantic-value shares among valid outputs with known critical extraction, one request occurrence per family×model. Unclear and other values remain in this all-known denominator. Polarity affirmative share is '+pct(f['fig_defaults']['polarity']['shares']['affirmative']['estimate'])+' (317/320). This descriptive all-output denominator differs from registered P3’s affirmative/negated directional share '+pct(p['P3']['affirmative_share']['estimate'])+' (317/319); the observed unclear output is outside the latter denominator. Balanced source pairs do not make ambiguous inputs informative about private intent.\n',
'## fig_channel_ladder\n\nP0 critical match across bare, +noncritical word, +critical chip, +all chips, and full source. Bare/noncrit indicate target-reference agreement, not accuracy. The supplied-cue channels evaluate critical preservation. Orange squares additionally require the joint partial contract for supplied general dimensions. The 78 speech-act families represent 55 recorded construction/seed clusters, not 78 independent constructions. Primary P1 uses complete pairs and therefore can differ slightly from subtraction of independently observed channel means.\n',
'## fig_cost_asymmetry\n\nNominal extra selections for the family’s modal bare reading versus its other target reading. Family default is the most frequent A/B value in P0 across four models, with P2/S3 as a tie-break; absent/tied defaults are excluded. P0 cost is zero for a matching top suggestion, otherwise the critical-chip count. P2 cost is zero for top-1, one for another matching suggestion, otherwise the critical-chip count. The fixed-roster modal default differs from the output-specific top-1 default used in nominal_action_cost.csv. Neither measure estimates typing time or guarantees successful repair.\n',
'## fig_politeness_ratchet\n\nP0 full-input plain→polite additions versus polite→plain removals, by model and pooled. Pooled '+str(p['P2']['addition']['n'])+' outputs per source register: 26 additions (8.12%) and six removals (1.88%). Registered paired addition−removal contrast is +6.25 pp [2.50,10.00], Holm-adjusted p='+f"{p['P2']['p_holm']:.6f}"+'. Pooled asymmetry does not describe every model: Qwen and Llama have more removals than additions. No P1 prompt or certainty-stratum data exist here; those discovery-only sensitivity rows/controls are omitted.\n',
'## fig_sets\n\nBare P2 versus S3 coverage@3: both source-pair values among the first three suggestions. P2 is one greedy request for three different meanings; S3 is three T=.7 draws. Unknown labels produce unknown sets unless both readings are already observed. Incomplete sets remain observed and flagged in the set audit. P2 increases polarity coverage by +7.19 pp [4.11,10.49], so the discovery “not polarity” clause does not repeat, despite low absolute polarity coverage. The figure reports marginal arm rates; paired differences use jointly observed sets and have their own denominator.\n',
'## fig_pipeline\n\nMethod schematic using the actual stored r2pol-001 P0 bare output from the first model in the fixed plotting order (GPT-6.1-terra): “I feel well.” The source, five rendered channels, output and extracted labels are read from stored specs/table. This is a lexicographically selected method illustration, not an independently selected failure-rate example; outcome-conditioned examples and their complete selection rules/rates are in analysis/r2c/examples.md.\n',
'## Reproduction\n\n```bash\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 .venv/bin/python paper/figs/make_figs.py --table runs/r2c1/scored.parquet --items \'data/items/r2_c[12].jsonl\' --out paper/figs/r2c --n-boot 10000 --seed 20261031 --cluster-by-items --strict-critical --exclude-primary\n.venv/bin/python analysis/r2c/write_figure_notes.py\n```\n']
(O/'CAPTIONS.md').write_text('\n'.join(text))
paths=[ROOT/'paper/figs/make_figs.py',ROOT/'runs/r2c1/scored.parquet',ROOT/'data/items/r2_c1.jsonl',ROOT/'data/items/r2_c2.jsonl']+sorted(O.glob('fig_*'))+[O/'CAPTIONS.md']
manifest={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in paths if p.is_file()}
(O/'provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Wrote captions and',len(manifest),'provenance hashes')
